\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{From commuting links to integers}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{For a regular connection with commuting links, \ref{fdip-015T} expresses
the index as a sum over connections on #{\mathbb C}. Their link values
have modulus one. So does the determinant of a unitary link on any
finite-dimensional fiber. Which integers can be read from products of these
numbers around plaquettes? Which are invariant under gauge transformations,
and when do parallel coordinate sections give the same integer?}
